I What and why
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

SMSQE  3.42 contains a new  scheduler mechanism for the  Qx0 machines, so that
specially prepared or executed	QLiberated  programs  run  correctly  on  that
platform, even if the machine is in COPYBACK mode.

For this,  SMSQE contains 4 new keywords QEXEC	and QEX, QEXEC_W and QEW (note
that QEX and QEW  are  just  shortened	versions  of  the  QEXEC  and  QEXEC_W
keywords, they add no additional facilities.)

QLiberated program must be started with one of these commands (unless they are
patched permanently).


II Starting QLiberated programs with the QEXEC (_w) commands
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=--=-=-=-=-=

The  QEXEC etc commands do not modify or patch the code of the program itself,
they just apply a small patch to the program's exception vector table.

As  can be expected, QEXEC and QEX do not suspend the calling job, QEXEC_W and
QEW do.

Admittedly,  these commands are pretty primitive.  They accept only two string
parameters:  the filename and a possible command line. The parameters need not
be between parentheses. The separator between parameters doesn't matter.

Example: QEXEC win1_program ; "command_line"

This  executes the program,  passing it a  possible command line  in the usual
way.

If  you start an (unpatched) QLiberated  program with anything else, including
launching  it from a file manager, that program will still crash as usual on a
Qx0 running in COPYBACK mode.


III Patching QLiberated programs permanently
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

The above commands exist to allow  for	an  occasional	use  of  a  QLiberated
program. If  you routinely  use a  QLiberated program,	you should  PATCH that
program. Once patched,	it may be started  with any of the  usual EXEC, EW etc
commands.

There is  a ready-made program allowing  you to apply a  patch to any program.
That program and the patch itself, however, are not part of SMSQE. They can be
downloaded from my site at

	 www.wlenerz.com/qlstuff

under the misc utilities section (Qx0_Qlibg_patch).

It is a zip file containing the patch, the patching program and documentation.


IV Not Qlib specific
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

The QEXEC  commands are NOT  specific to QLiberated  programs, potentially any
other program  that would  crash when  the Qx0	is in  COPYBACK mode,  but run
normally when in WRITETHROUGH mode, may be started with these commands.

The QEXEC etc commands do NOT modify the QLiberated (or other) program in such
a  way that the program could run in COPYBACK mode. Rather, whenever a QEXEC'd
program gets a slice of  CPU  time  by	the  scheduler,  the  CPU  is  put  in
WRITETHROUGH  mode and then put  back into COPYBACK mode  when that program is
suspended by the scheduler and another program gets its time slice& This means
that a patched progam will NOT run at the full COPYBACK speed.


V COPYBACK always on
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

As a  result of  this new  scheduler policy,  Qx0 machines  now always	run in
COPYBACK mode. The different  keywords	(SERIALIZED,  WRITETHROUGH,  COPYBACK)
still exist for compatibility reasons, but they have no effect any more.


